  "rawText": "She married Vernal Davis and continued to make her home in Washington, D.C.. In 1950, when her sister, Eula Mae, became ill and could not care for her infant son, Exrtie Lee took over his care. Eula Mae passed away in October of that same year and the baby (Woody) was left with Extie Lee and Vernal permanently. In the mid sixties, when Woody was old enough to be left alone after school, Extie Lee accepted a position with The Department of The United States Treasury. Even though, she retained her membership in Daniel Chapel Babtist Church, she was very active in several churches in the Washington area. She and Vernal moved to their new home in Enfield, North Carolina, in 1980. He passed away in 1987, and she followed him in 1991. Her goal in life was to be a good Christian. Front Row: Robert Calvin, Extie Lee, Maurice Back Row: Mattie, Pearl C. Eula Mae and Lillie Bell (Sweet)",
